# R5 risky surfaces — a PR touching ANY of these requires both adversarial
# auditors (audit/grok + audit/gatekeeper) to post a success commit status
# before it can merge. The r5-audit-gate workflow enforces this mechanically.
#
# DESIGN: broad GLOBS that DEFAULT-COVER (fail-closed), NOT an enumerated
# allowlist that silently drifts as new modules are added (Gatekeeper PR#57
# BLOCK: an allowlist omitting gate_runner/plan_loader/chat_layer/ui app.js —
# each of which had a real bug — would false-green an un-audited PR). Better to
# over-gate (a trivial change asks for a fast ENDORSE) than under-gate (skip the
# audit on a risky file). One glob per line; '#' and blank lines ignored.
#
# All orchestrator package code (fleet-core; bug here = fleet-wide blast radius):
fleet_orchestrator/*.py
# The dashboard / wake-packet render surface (XSS class):
ui/static/*.js
ui/*.html
# CI/gate config itself (self-protecting — a PR weakening the gate is gated):
.github/workflows/*.yml
.github/r5-risky-paths
scripts/r5-risk-classifier
# Packaging / entrypoint + the installed CLIs:
setup.py
scripts/orch-*
scripts/taey-*
